htmlcov/

# Your CV, your profile, and everything built from them. None of it belongs to
# this repo and none of it should ever reach a fork of it.
#
# This is the first of three layers, and the weakest: .gitignore is advisory,
# so .githooks/pre-commit refuses the commit and CI checks the tracked file
# list. Across ten forks one `git add -f` is inevitable.
# `jobhunt/` is where a workspace lands now. /cv, /runs and /profile.yaml are
# the layout this used to have, kept ignored so an older checkout cannot commit
# one by accident.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: `plugins/jobhunt/` is the shipped
# plugin and must stay tracked. An unanchored `jobhunt/` would swallow it.
/jobhunt/
/cv/
/runs/
/profile.yaml
.env
*.pdf
*.docx
